From 64b17e1ea7c8e42ce92fcc54c34309c4a60f4371 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 00:57:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cli): harden fb-lane against shell command injection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

runGit() built commands as `git ${args}` and handed them to execSync,
so anything woven into a branch name, commit message, task ID, or lane —
including values that arrive over the MCP server as untrusted tool
arguments — was interpreted by a shell. A lane like "tech;rm -rf ~ #"
became a branch name and then executed arbitrary commands.

- Run git via execFileSync('git', argv) with no shell; convert every
  call site that interpolates caller data to pass an args array.
- Replace the shell `||` fallback in submit with a JS try/catch.
- Run the doctor's lsof lookup through execFileSync as well.
- Validate task IDs and lane names against strict allowlists at both the
  CLI and MCP entry points, and refuse option-like ("-"-prefixed) branch
  names before they reach git.
- Make the script importable (guard main(), export helpers) and add
  tools/fb-lane.test.cjs covering the validators and proving shell
  metacharacters in arguments are inert.
- Resync the bundled plugin copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015d6nhofKQPZcEt15XBePE1
